# Worktrees start at latest origin/develop

Cursor worktrees default to **current HEAD**. Local `develop` is often dozens of commits behind `origin/develop`. Do not create a worktree from HEAD.

`.cursor/worktrees.json` hard-resets Cursor-created worktrees to fetched `origin/develop`. Agents creating worktrees by hand must do the same:

```bash
git fetch origin develop
git worktree add -b <name> .worktrees/<name-with-slashes-as-hyphens> origin/develop
```

```bash
# BAD — branches from whatever this checkout is
git worktree add -b <name> .worktrees/<name>
```
